&=\\left\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2\\,|\\,x \\neq 0\\right\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707964 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d4c90f8-404c-5b25-ab6b-319c0caac737" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2\\,|\\,x - 1 \\leq 0\\right\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707952} {:answer/id #uuid "69924fe4-3eaa-528b-800b-83b7181ac78d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2\\,|\\,x - 1 \\neq 0\\right\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707959} {:answer/id #uuid "d1f94c98-6615-5a8a-9bd8-655b11349ea6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2\\,|\\,x - 1 \\geq 0\\right\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707969} {:answer/id #uuid "d9c16d50-14ee-501c-ad78-05cc61fe3e17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2\\,|\\,x - 1 < 0\\right\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707971} {:answer/id #uuid "e900ac7a-9e37-575f-8a06-31fac4c13425" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\mathbb R^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707975}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d1f94c98-6615-5a8a-9bd8-655b11349ea6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2\\,|\\,x - 1 \\geq 0\\right\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707969} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0b30e45-fe82-5225-9127-1f5a3f69fa4f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707963}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a1df36c2-51de-5855-bf79-3d8245154fb9" :question/problem "Determine the domain of the real vector field\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=\\sqrt{x - 1}\\,i+\\left(y^{2}\\right)\\,j.\n$$\n\nRemember: both component functions must be defined." :question/worked-solution "Write $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x,y)&=\\sqrt{x - 1}\\\\Q(x,y)&=y^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nP: A real square root requires a nonnegative radicand.\n\nThe required conditions are $x - 1 \\geq 0$.\n\nThus $D_P=\\left\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2\\,|\\,x - 1 \\geq 0\\right\\}$.\n\nQ: This polynomial is defined everywhere in the real plane.\n\nThus $D_Q=\\mathbb R^2$.\n\nThe domain is the intersection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D&=D_P\\cap D_Q\\\\&=\\left\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2\\,|\\,x - 1 \\geq 0\\right\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708013 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a225254-d2c6-5337-a636-e35c15a56a3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707999} {:answer/id #uuid "a26eb61a-d4b2-5866-a966-e0ec2bb41eca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708027}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a225254-d2c6-5337-a636-e35c15a56a3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707999} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b6be1fd-8a2c-5e3a-ad0b-7a15b9190b67" :answer-field/key "$Q(x,y)=\\langle \\frac{1}{x}, y^2\\rangle$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708004} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6e1fada-9084-5f5b-9020-d751877d347d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708029} {:answer/id #uuid "fcb3ead8-6bd5-5775-a445-30d4d2672c23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708046}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fcb3ead8-6bd5-5775-a445-30d4d2672c23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708046} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0805a02-937d-5b70-b065-8ff8e99b491f" :answer-field/key "$T(x,y,z)=(\\sin(x))\\,\\mathbf i+(\\cos(y))\\,\\mathbf j+(\\cot(z))\\,\\mathbf k$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708026} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11471394-6e12-52ef-a207-16f492a0c7c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708002} {:answer/id #uuid "efc162ed-acf7-5ac4-8033-f764527cbb15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708045}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "efc162ed-acf7-5ac4-8033-f764527cbb15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708045} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb3a3811-3c7b-5cde-bf39-b86324d757ca" :answer-field/key "$Y(x,y,z)=\\sin(x)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708043}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6eae2a66-d9c5-52d7-973f-377c00bb51c6" :question/problem "A vector field on $\\mathbb R^3$ assigns a vector in $\\mathbb R^3$ to each point of a subset of $\\mathbb R^3$.\n\nWhich of the following are vector fields on $\\mathbb R^3$? Use each function's natural real domain. Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A vector field on $\\mathbb R^3$ assigns a vector in $\\mathbb R^3$ to each point of a subset of $\\mathbb R^3$.\n\nCheck each function's declared inputs and output vectors.\n\n- **T.** $T(x,y,z)$ takes points in $\\mathbb R^3$. Its three standard-basis coefficients give \n$$\nT(x,y,z)=\\langle \\sin(x), \\cos(y), \\cot(z)\\rangle.\n$$\nExclude the poles of the trigonometric component. Its natural domain is\n$$\nS_{T}=\\{(x,y,z)\\in \\mathbb R^3\\mid z\\ne k\\pi,\\ k\\in\\mathbb Z\\}.\n$$\nIt maps its nonempty domain in $\\mathbb R^3$ to vectors in $\\mathbb R^3$, so it **is** a vector field on $\\mathbb R^3$.\n\n- **Q.** $Q(x,y)$ takes points in $\\mathbb R^2$. Its output has $2$ coordinates and is a vector in $\\mathbb R^2$. A denominator must be nonzero. Its natural domain is\n$$\nS_{Q}=\\{(x,y)\\in \\mathbb R^2\\mid x\\ne0\\}.\n$$\nIt **is not** a vector field on $\\mathbb R^3$ because its declared inputs are not points of $\\mathbb R^3$ and its outputs are not vectors in $\\mathbb R^3$.\n\n- **Y.** $Y(x,y,z)$ takes points in $\\mathbb R^3$. Its output $\\sin(x)$ is a scalar in $\\mathbb R$. All components are defined on $\\mathbb R^3$. It **is not** a vector field on $\\mathbb R^3$ because its outputs are not vectors in $\\mathbb R^3$.\n\nSelect $T$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708014 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29420350-aa17-584d-a333-52a7c7d9d286" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708006} {:answer/id #uuid "82c903e6-70fb-51d6-b590-a59f3c55eeab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708021}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29420350-aa17-584d-a333-52a7c7d9d286" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708006} :answer-field/id #uuid "39c0cd14-a81f-539f-8daf-b152867e3005" :answer-field/key "$U(x,y,z)=\\left(\\frac{1}{x+1}\\right)\\,\\mathbf i+(y^2)\\,\\mathbf j+\\left(\\frac{z}{y+1}\\right)\\,\\mathbf k$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708007} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "806c210a-2def-5c1b-8a03-96a12517eb5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708017} {:answer/id #uuid "fd804ac1-54b8-5e42-80db-b60141b8d3ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708047}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "806c210a-2def-5c1b-8a03-96a12517eb5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708017} :answer-field/id #uuid "3eb69669-b272-5476-bb7d-80afd7340fe4" :answer-field/key "$M(x,y,z)=\\langle x+2, y^2, z+x\\rangle$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708008} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82c0ebbc-4a48-5528-916c-34a97eb60772" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708020} {:answer/id #uuid "98bac681-7763-5876-adbd-dfbbff33fd58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708024}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98bac681-7763-5876-adbd-dfbbff33fd58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708024} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e9038ec-5b24-5a1e-9878-eba5450bfb16" :answer-field/key "$S(x,y)=\\langle \\ln(y-1), \\sqrt{x-1}\\rangle$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708025}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6f871634-2896-5f28-a432-eb07d2e8419b" :question/problem "A vector field on $\\mathbb R^3$ assigns a vector in $\\mathbb R^3$ to each point of a subset of $\\mathbb R^3$.\n\nWhich of the following are vector fields on $\\mathbb R^3$? Use each function's natural real domain. Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A vector field on $\\mathbb R^3$ assigns a vector in $\\mathbb R^3$ to each point of a subset of $\\mathbb R^3$.\n\nCheck each function's declared inputs and output vectors.\n\n- **M.** $M(x,y,z)$ takes points in $\\mathbb R^3$. Its output has $3$ coordinates and is a vector in $\\mathbb R^3$. All components are defined on $\\mathbb R^3$. It maps its nonempty domain in $\\mathbb R^3$ to vectors in $\\mathbb R^3$, so it **is** a vector field on $\\mathbb R^3$.\n\n- **S.** $S(x,y)$ takes points in $\\mathbb R^2$. Its output has $2$ coordinates and is a vector in $\\mathbb R^2$. A logarithm needs a positive argument. A square root allows a zero radicand. Its natural domain is\n$$\nS_{S}=\\{(x,y)\\in \\mathbb R^2\\mid y-1>0,\\quad x-1\\ge0\\}.\n$$\nIt **is not** a vector field on $\\mathbb R^3$ because its declared inputs are not points of $\\mathbb R^3$ and its outputs are not vectors in $\\mathbb R^3$.\n\n- **U.** $U(x,y,z)$ takes points in $\\mathbb R^3$. Its three standard-basis coefficients give \n$$\nU(x,y,z)=\\langle \\frac{1}{x+1}, y^2, \\frac{z}{y+1}\\rangle.\n$$\nA denominator must be nonzero. Its natural domain is\n$$\nS_{U}=\\{(x,y,z)\\in \\mathbb R^3\\mid x+1\\ne0,\\quad y+1\\ne0\\}.\n$$\nIt maps its nonempty domain in $\\mathbb R^3$ to vectors in $\\mathbb R^3$, so it **is** a vector field on $\\mathbb R^3$.\n\nSelect $M$ and $U$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708019 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41d14073-9f23-54b6-865d-38f5269fb7ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708009} {:answer/id #uuid "934774aa-e79b-5421-b245-402fde1a4466" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708023}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93477