5} {:answer/id #uuid "b2da2c93-7184-5bb2-9ca8-64227a731de3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708032}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78bf3b76-3c82-5499-ae81-901b212d459b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708015} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4f71ee6-8329-5efd-8d4d-499e8bf421ee" :answer-field/key "$U(t)=\\langle \\ln(t+2), \\sqrt{t+2}, t^2\\rangle$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708028}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e0a1d6cc-b162-5d47-9332-63fcc8245112" :question/problem "A vector field on $\\mathbb R^3$ assigns a vector in $\\mathbb R^3$ to each point of a subset of $\\mathbb R^3$.\n\nWhich of the following are vector fields on $\\mathbb R^3$? Use each function's natural real domain. Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A vector field on $\\mathbb R^3$ assigns a vector in $\\mathbb R^3$ to each point of a subset of $\\mathbb R^3$.\n\nCheck each function's declared inputs and output vectors.\n\n- **H.** $H(x,y)$ takes points in $\\mathbb R^2$. Its output has $2$ coordinates and is a vector in $\\mathbb R^2$. A denominator must be nonzero. Its natural domain is\n$$\nS_{H}=\\{(x,y)\\in \\mathbb R^2\\mid x+1\\ne0\\}.\n$$\nIt **is not** a vector field on $\\mathbb R^3$ because its declared inputs are not points of $\\mathbb R^3$ and its outputs are not vectors in $\\mathbb R^3$.\n\n- **Y.** $Y(x,y,z)$ takes points in $\\mathbb R^3$. Its three standard-basis coefficients give \n$$\nY(x,y,z)=\\langle \\ln(y), \\sqrt{x}, z^2\\rangle.\n$$\nA logarithm needs a positive argument. A square root allows a zero radicand. Its natural domain is\n$$\nS_{Y}=\\{(x,y,z)\\in \\mathbb R^3\\mid y>0,\\quad x\\ge0\\}.\n$$\nIt maps its nonempty domain in $\\mathbb R^3$ to vectors in $\\mathbb R^3$, so it **is** a vector field on $\\mathbb R^3$.\n\n- **U.** $U(t)$ takes one real parameter. Its output has $3$ coordinates and is a vector in $\\mathbb R^3$. A logarithm needs a positive argument. A square root allows a zero radicand. Its natural domain is\n$$\nS_{U}=\\{(t)\\in \\mathbb R\\mid t+2>0,\\quad t+2\\ge0\\}.\n$$\nIt **is not** a vector field on $\\mathbb R^3$ because its declared inputs are not points of $\\mathbb R^3$.\n\nSelect $Y$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708083 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "891c7913-f010-50f4-99c6-48e4299a76e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708077} {:answer/id #uuid "b37fdf7b-f430-5cc7-9e50-fac83fd05f36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708082}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "891c7913-f010-50f4-99c6-48e4299a76e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708077} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e12282b-9708-53a1-b904-7dcdec083335" :answer-field/key "$L(x,y,z)=\\langle e^{x}, xe^{y}\\rangle$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708076} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "abfbe0f5-fa7b-54a7-9ac4-076beb1395e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708081} {:answer/id #uuid "d1ec6035-ca2e-59a0-885d-ed3a5ca607e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708084}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "abfbe0f5-fa7b-54a7-9ac4-076beb1395e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708081} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a8b10a1-b5eb-5874-98fb-895aa2df6fbd" :answer-field/key "$A(x,y,z)=\\begin{bmatrix}e^{x} \\\\ xe^{y} \\\\ z^2\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708078} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c070b61-5d62-5e22-997c-5f96a08615a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708075} {:answer/id #uuid "8b22d99f-281e-512f-a1b2-d85f2df87145" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708079}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b22d99f-281e-512f-a1b2-d85f2df87145" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708079} :answer-field/id #uuid "97843882-d0ea-5ee1-bd92-9f334c43b270" :answer-field/key "$R(x,y,z)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\ln(y) \\\\ \\sqrt{x}\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708080}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bb48724e-a95c-5176-953a-760a90efc6d9" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on $\\mathbb R^3$? Use each function's natural real domain. Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A vector field on $\\mathbb R^3$ assigns a vector in $\\mathbb R^3$ to each point of a subset of $\\mathbb R^3$.\n\nCheck each function's declared inputs and output vectors.\n\n- **A.** $A(x,y,z)$ takes points in $\\mathbb R^3$. Its output has $3$ coordinates and is a vector in $\\mathbb R^3$. All components are defined on $\\mathbb R^3$. It maps its nonempty domain in $\\mathbb R^3$ to vectors in $\\mathbb R^3$, so it **is** a vector field on $\\mathbb R^3$.\n\n- **R.** $R(x,y,z)$ takes points in $\\mathbb R^3$. Its output has $2$ coordinates and is a vector in $\\mathbb R^2$. A logarithm needs a positive argument. A square root allows a zero radicand. Its natural domain is\n$$\nS_{R}=\\{(x,y,z)\\in \\mathbb R^3\\mid y>0,\\quad x\\ge0\\}.\n$$\nIt **is not** a vector field on $\\mathbb R^3$ because its outputs are not vectors in $\\mathbb R^3$.\n\n- **L.** $L(x,y,z)$ takes points in $\\mathbb R^3$. Its output has $2$ coordinates and is a vector in $\\mathbb R^2$. All components are defined on $\\mathbb R^3$. It **is not** a vector field on $\\mathbb R^3$ because its outputs are not vectors in $\\mathbb R^3$.\n\nSelect $A$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712187 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04a46fda-d6d2-51b0-9668-2e5812b49e7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\pi}\\sqrt{1+t^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712176} {:answer/id #uuid "060fe18d-6ac7-54a1-a34b-21fc3ee3f537" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\pi/2}\\sqrt{1+2t^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712177} {:answer/id #uuid "0f98f770-a92b-5c90-b033-e29f682c819f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\pi/2}\\sqrt{2+t^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712178} {:answer/id #uuid "3ceac499-bd55-56ad-952d-4afcf19d85fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\pi/2}\\sqrt{t^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712182} {:answer/id #uuid "babbc2f8-61c7-5d4d-943f-9a6ce7a55394" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\pi/2}\\sqrt{1+t^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712190}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "babbc2f8-61c7-5d4d-943f-9a6ce7a55394" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\pi/2}\\sqrt{1+t^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712190} :answer-field/id #uuid "c69e08d9-5850-502b-a5f5-58a76caeb4ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712192}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a2a7d829-e85e-5347-ae05-728a609ee238" :question/problem "Which integral expression gives the arc length of the curve\n$$\n\\mathbf g(t)=\\langle t\\cos t,\\,1+t\\sin t\\rangle\n$$\nfrom $t=0$ to $t=\\pi/2$? Do not evaluate the integral.\n\n![The planar spiral segment with its parameter endpoints and direction of travel.](images/68/689af73f5d8a1f08682e5e56feefbbeb8337ee28cd352815af43c6c8cb32c369.png)" :question/worked-solution "Apply the product rule in both components; the constant $1$ differentiates to zero:\n$$\n\\mathbf g'(t)=\\langle\\cos t-t\\sin t,\\,\\sin t+t\\cos t\\rangle.\n$$\nSquare the two components and add:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\|\\mathbf g'(t)\\|^2\n&=(\\cos t-t\\sin t)^2+(\\sin t+t\\cos t)^2\\\\\n&=\\cos^2t-2t\\sin t\\cos t+t^2\\sin^2t\\\\\n&\\quad+\\sin^2t+2t\\sin t\\cos t+t^2\\cos^2t\\\\\n&=(\\cos^2t+\\sin^2t)+t^2(\\sin^2t+\\cos^2t)\\\\\n&=1+t^2.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThe mixed terms cancel. Taking the nonnegative square root and retaining the parameter bounds, we obtain\n$$\nL=\\int_0^{\\pi/2}\\|\\mathbf g'(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t\n=\\int_0^{\\pi/2}\\sqrt{1+t^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712188 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21b31ca6-47eb-5311-8af6-2850bc6f80f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{1}e^{2t}\\sqrt{t^2+2t+6}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712180} {:answer/id #uuid "475303d4-2229-5125-9c0f-a60bd1c4e7e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{1}e^t\\sqrt{t^2+2t+6}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712184} {:answer/id #uuid "68afdc4f-44ca-5ac2-9ca2-ab24f1c701cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{1}e^t\\sqrt{t^2+5}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712185} {:answer/id #uuid "d04382ac-4dab-508a-ace0-6d770262978a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{2}e^t\\sqrt{t^2+2t+6}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712194} {:answer/id #uuid "fd32c773-3977-55be-93e4-2c4dc5bb92b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{1}e^t\\sqrt{t^2+2t+3}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712195}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "475303d4-2229-5125-9c0f-a60bd1c4e7e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{1}e^t\\sqrt{t^2+2t+6}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712184} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff1837c1-38ff-5624-bb7a-92ab97f229fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712196}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a56b482d-f39d-5a0b-aaf4-c3620d8a8793" :question/problem "Which integral expression gives the arc length of the spatial curve\n$$\n\\mathbf f(t)=\\langle e^t\\cos(2t),\\,e^t\\sin(2t),\\,t e^t\\rangle\n$$\nfrom $t=0$ to $t=1$? Do not evaluate the integral.\n\n![The spatial curve with its parameter endpoints and direction of travel.](images/51/51cf2056fa2270172cefa8d198a600d0486fb884605c93521c9df7c614846e87.png)" :question/worked-solution "Use the product rule in all three components and the chain rule for the angle $2t$:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_x'(t)&=e^t(\\cos(2t)-2\\sin(2t)),\\\\\nf_y'(t)&=e^t(\\sin(2t)+2\\cos(2t)),\\\\\nf_z'(t)&=e^t(t+1).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nTo simplify its magnitude, first expand the two trigonometric squares:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&(\\cos(2t)-2\\sin(2t))^2+(\\sin(2t)+2\\cos(2t))^2\\\\\n&\\quad=\\cos^2(2t)-4\\sin(2t)\\cos(2t)+4\\sin^2(2t)\\\\\n&\\qquad+\\sin^2(2t)+4\\sin(2t)\\cos(2t)+4\\cos^2(2t)\\\\\n&\\quad=5(\\sin^2(2t)+\\cos^2(2t))=5.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nInclude the third derivative component when forming the speed:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\|\\mathbf f'(t)\\|\n&=\\sqrt{e^{2t}\\bigl(5+(t+1)^2\\bigr)}\\\\\n&=e^t\\sqrt{t^2+2t+6}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nHere $\\sqrt{e^{2t}}=e^t$ because $e^t>0$. Therefore,\n$$\nL=\\int_0^1\\|\\mathbf f'(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t\n=\\int_0^1 e^t\\sqrt{t^2+2t+6}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712189 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d87d15d-22f7-52ad-aec8-213294a2535f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\pi/4}\\sqrt{\\sin^2(3t)+\\cos^2(2t)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712179} {:answer/id #uuid "2c887878-af59-592e-bd5e-e75e44a31fbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\pi/2}\\sqrt{9\\cos^2(3t)+4\\sin^2(2t)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712181} {:answer/id #uuid "46525687-9aea-51a0-b13a-8466aa3a09e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\pi/4}\\sqrt{9\\cos^2(3t)+4\\sin^2(2t)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712183} {:answer/id #uuid "8fc29e20-a8b7-5445-9014-a35de5c14dae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\pi/4}\\sqrt{9\\sin^2(3t)+4\\cos^2(2t)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712186} {:answer/id #uuid "cf7968a9-c02f-5c86-8706-f4b1d391e1ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\pi/4}\\sqrt{3\\cos^2(3t)+2\\sin^2(2t)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712193}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46525687-9aea-51a0-b13a-8466aa3a09e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\pi/4}\\sqrt{9\\cos^2(3t)+4\\sin^2(2t)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712183} :answer-field/id #uuid "c42aa143-3a87-5d3a-b345-6558c5e7ef1c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712191}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b564c4ef-2f95-5927-97f2-a4136bc14d49" :question/problem "Which integral expression gives the arc length of the curve\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle\\sin(3t),\\,\\cos(2t)\\rangle\n$$\nfrom $t=0$ to $t=\\pi/4$? Do not evaluate the integral.\n\n![The planar curve with its parameter endpoints and direction of travel.](images/39/39f59b0f1d6f6df41d552f082b3b05c186f934b39cfd87da8e6208d48f66f989.png)" :question/worked-solution "Differentiate each component, including the inner factors $3$ and $2$:\n$$\n\\mathbf r'(t)=\\langle3\\cos(3t),\\,-2\\sin(2t)\\rangle.\n$$\nThe speed is the magnitude of this derivative:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(3\\cos(3t))^2+(-2\\sin(2t))^2}\\\\\n&=\\sqrt{9\\cos^2(3t)+4\\sin^2(2t)}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nBoth derivative components are squared, so the negative sign in the second component contributes a positive term. Retaining the given parameter bounds gives\n$$\nL=\\int_0^{\\pi/4}\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t\n=\\int_0^{\\pi/4}\\sqrt{9\\cos^2(3t)+4\\sin^2(2t)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712222 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38650951-5c73-5b06-a103-957fea977740" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{84}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712223} {:answer/id #uuid "49b45ecf-f13a-5e28-a9da-e7da1ba6f7a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712225} {:answer/id #uuid "6ce4a2ce-365f-5e14-8d8a-8b49e4ce90b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712227} {:answer/id #uuid "913edae9-38fe-5f67-a923-97bf97e9520c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712228} {:answer/id #uuid "a4542fd3-48f8-5d9a-a601-00346228d618" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712229}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "913edae9-38fe-5f67-a923-97bf97e9520c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712228} :answer-field/id #uuid "f7100075-2d08-5bea-873d-6ece59d33907" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712237}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "35c0e8f7-e3f6-5691-9a25-51356b421a25" :question/problem "![The specified curve segment is blue; its continuation is red.](images/e1/e1986870b945ca2f5337b1d33b1d911af9e73cf2369876a8d92cea2aa0e8e067.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle t^3-3t,\\,3t^2\\rangle\n$$\n\nfrom $t=0$ to $t=1$." :question/worked-solution "First, differentiate each component and compute the speed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf r'(t)&=\\langle 3t^2-3,\\,6t\\rangle,\\\\\n\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(3t^2-3)^2+(6t)^2}\\\\\n&=\\sqrt{9t^4-18t^2+9+36t^2}\\\\\n&=\\sqrt{9(t^2+1)^2}\\\\\n&=3(t^2+1).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe last step uses $t^2+1>0$. Integrate the speed over the given parameter interval:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL&=\\int_0^1\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\\n&=\\int_0^1 3(t^2+1)\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\\n&=\\left[t^3+3t\\right]_0^1\\\\\n&=4.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712232 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ffd5dec-d31d-5613-8a90-3a9decde37ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16-4\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712218} {:answer/id #uuid "236598d8-45ca-5a83-b20b-bb53fe342f4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12+4\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712220} {:answer/id #uuid "a8840a95-8378-5885-a2b5-44e48836f02c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\sqrt{2}-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712230} {:answer/id #uuid "b4919106-b27e-5d24-8099-0fe44bc4575b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16+4\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712233} {:answer/id #uuid "cbd843fa-f5e4-5114-8a3b-89c6e027eb19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712235}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "236598d8-45ca-5a83-b20b-bb53fe342f4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12+4\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712220} :answer-field/id #uuid "48ced425-4b60-5c4f-9f8e-24274fe6264a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712224}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b3bad0e0-f8b7-57a2-9b46-d4f38ae11151" :question/problem "![The specified curve segment is blue; its continuation is red.](images/85/8502d80ae296e43f03f417781d54ce777f34eb34fef69db4df0bf09119d14d39.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle 7-2t^3,\\,3t^2+10\\rangle\n$$\n\nfrom $t=-1$ to $t=\\sqrt{3}$." :question/worked-solution "First, differentiate each component and compute the speed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf r'(t)&=\\langle -6t^2,\\,6t\\rangle,\\\\\n\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{36t^4+36t^2}\\\\\n&=6\\sqrt{t^2(t^2+1)}\\\\\n&=6|t|\\sqrt{t^2+1}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSpeed is nonnegative. Since $|t|=-t$ on $[-1,0]$ and $|t|=t$ on $[0,\\sqrt{3}]$, split the integral at $t=0$:\n\n$$\nL=\\int_{-1}^0 -6t\\sqrt{t^2+1}\\,\\mathrm{d}t\n  +\\int_0^{\\sqrt{3}}6t\\sqrt{t^2+1}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nFor each integral use $u=t^2+1$, with $\\mathrm{d}u=2t\\,\\mathrm{d}t$. On the first interval $u$ decreases from $2$ to $1$; on the second it increases from $1$ to $4$. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL&=-3\\int_2^1 u^{1/2}\\,\\mathrm{d}u+3\\int_1^4 u^{1/2}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\\\\n&=-\\left[2u^{3/2}\\right]_2^1+\\left[2u^{3/2}\\right]_1^4\\\\\n&=(4\\sqrt{2}-2)+(16-2)\\\\\n&=12+4\\sqrt{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBoth pieces contribute positive length. Replacing $|t|$ by $t$ on the whole interval would subtract the first piece instead of adding it."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712236 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30c46591-36ab-5e63-8ced-239fadad3ee1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712221} {:answer/id #uuid "4aaf8200-7e42-5871-8e88-34c44b6676e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712226} {:answer/id #uuid "b194b2cd-5d0d-5226-b2d1-425f1fc06fec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{96}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712231} {:answer/id #uuid "c733c09b-3171-5cec-ab10-159735dbd1f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\sqrt{2}-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712234} {:answer/id #uuid "feaf613f-9b50-5fde-a4d8-a87965e4dd61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{2}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712238}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "feaf613f-9b50-5fde-a4d8-a87965e4dd61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{2}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712238} :answer-field/id #uuid "1503605a-d4e6-5a30-819c-4cb14aca7f6c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712219}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d78ce1b2-1835-5a0e-bdab-f576c73b68db" :question/problem "![The specified curve segment is blue; its continuation is red.](images/d4/d4f2c2141b391c380e44a40f17ba537bfb1b9ce4b26acb6ef8d38fb3bdd3421c.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle 7-2t^3,\\,3t^2+10\\rangle\n$$\n\nfrom $t=0$ to $t=1$." :question/worked-solution "First, differentiate each component and compute the speed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf r'(t)&=\\langle -6t^2,\\,6t\\rangle,\\\\\n\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{36t^4+36t^2}\\\\\n&=6|t|\\sqrt{t^2+1}\\\\\n&=6t\\sqrt{t^2+1}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere $t\\geq0$ on $[0,1]$, so $|t|=t$. Thus\n\n$$\nL=\\int_0^1 6t\\sqrt{t^2+1}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nUse $u=t^2+1$, so $\\mathrm{d}u=2t\\,\\mathrm{d}t$. The bounds become $u=1$ and $u=2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nL&=3\\int_1^2 u^{1/2}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\\\\n&=\\left[2u^{3/2}\\right]_1^2\\\\\n&=2(2\\sqrt{2}-1)\\\\\n&=4\\sqrt{2}-2.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712650 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "601557a4-53f7-5ec8-aa93-aef5db0e573f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{1}2 \\sqrt{2} \\sqrt{2 t^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712656} {:answer/id #uuid "6839d844-d9bb-500b-82c1-c862aa50e036" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{1}2 \\sqrt{4 t^{2} + \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712660} {:answer/id #uuid "7fa62366-75f5-5431-b810-e2ca95e536f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{1}2 \\sqrt{4 t^{2} - \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712663} {:answer/id #uuid "ac178b76-24d4-56e7-a6c3-f2c541d46ff0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{1}2 \\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712670} {:answer/id #uuid "fc971660-ec23-5707-b005-f75f66f4e341" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{1}2 \\sqrt{8 t^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712684}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ac178b76-24d4-56e7-a6c3-f2c541d46ff0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{1}2 \\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712670} :answer-field/id #uuid "69f174a1-3db0-5a3d-aa23-9c9ab1bc2be6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712661}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "01286228-4d4a-5791-808e-e16e2aff9197" :question/problem "Which integral expression gives the arc length of the curve\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle 2 t^{2},\\,- 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},\\,2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\rangle\n$$\nfrom $t=-1$ to $t=1$? Do not evaluate the integral." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate each coordinate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r_{x}'(t) & =4 t \\\\ r_{y}'(t) & =2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\\\ r_{z}'(t) & =2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquare each derivative component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S_{x} & =16 t^{2} \\\\ S_{y} & =4 \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} \\\\ S_{z} & =4 \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombine paired squares using $\\sin^2(t)+\\cos^2(t)=1$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\| & =\\sqrt{S_x+S_y+S_z} \\\\  & =2 \\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRetain the parameter bounds and integrate the speed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =\\int_{-1}^{1}\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\  & =\\int_{-1}^{1}2 \\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712657 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2972c07d-e9e9-599e-89ce-d723a640ca8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{16 t^{8} + 9 t^{6} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712654} {:answer/id #uuid "6bf8edc3-e624-5038-b9b7-35fbf3939214" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{32 t^{6} + 9 t^{4} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712662} {:answer/id #uuid "b2ae85dc-b60c-5aec-8d08-766f21270fbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{1}t^{2} \\sqrt{16 t^{2} + 9}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712673} {:answer/id #uuid "bd72888e-d5c7-5d66-ace8-0b07b20c700e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{16 t^{6} + 9 t^{4} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712674} {:answer/id #uuid "f4b270eb-3c76-5575-9e97-7c702a4471dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{16 t^{6} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712680}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd72888e-d5c7-5d66-ace8-0b07b20c700e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{16 t^{6} + 9 t^{4} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712674} :answer-field/id #uuid "679edefe-726a-599a-b430-4f5ee50cb6b4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712659}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "615a769a-3f2d-5f9b-a9f7-5c7814b14059" :question/problem "Which integral expression gives the arc length of the curve\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=(- t^{3})\\,i+(t)\\,j+(- t^{4})\\,k\n$$\nfrom $t=-1$ to $t=1$? Do not evaluate the integral." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate each coordinate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r_{x}'(t) & =- 3 t^{2} \\\\ r_{y}'(t) & =1 \\\\ r_{z}'(t) & =- 4 t^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquare each derivative component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S_{x} & =9 t^{4} \\\\ S_{y} & =1 \\\\ S_{z} & =16 t^{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\| & =\\sqrt{S_x+S_y+S_z} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16 t^{6} + 9 t^{4} + 1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRetain the parameter bounds and integrate the speed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =\\int_{-1}^{1}\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\  & =\\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{16 t^{6} + 9 t^{4} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712664 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "259ba87f-e1e6-5ee5-8459-b2b47baafd41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}2 \\sqrt{\\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 4 \\cos^{2}{\\left(2 t \\right)}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712652} {:answer/id #uuid "26345ed5-5065-5a43-804d-c9fa22c46fd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}2 \\left|{\\cos{\\left(t \\right)}}\\right|\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712653} {:answer/id #uuid "852bedbd-f11b-5cfe-a3eb-a9afea1dbb00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}2 \\sqrt{\\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\cos^{2}{\\left(2 t \\right)}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712665} {:answer/id #uuid "ad7b390c-594f-5fd2-bd57-a90633c3e24f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}2 \\sqrt{\\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 16 \\cos^{2}{\\left(2 t \\right)}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712672} {:answer/id #uuid "f097230e-3680-5961-941a-4afe5cc393d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}2 \\sqrt{2} \\sqrt{\\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\cos^{2}{\\left(2 t \\right)}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712678}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "259ba87f-e1e6-5ee5-8459-b2b47baafd41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}2 \\sqrt{\\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 4 \\cos^{2}{\\left(2 t \\right)}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712652} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6d93c03-ac86-5ed3-b846-ee56eef4d526" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712681}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "81dd0ebc-9ec1-55a6-a58e-f3e7773d35f1" :question/problem "Which integral expression gives the arc length of the curve\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle 2 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)},\\,2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\rangle\n$$\nfrom $t=0$ to $t=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$? Do not evaluate the integral.\n\n![The curve segment, parameter endpoints, and direction of travel.](images/9a/9af74cb2e6eb90342024f67f39b5e46b746d350ccb249af4390d45fbc058a91c.png)" :question/worked-solution "Differentiate each coordinate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r_{x}'(t) & =4 \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)} \\\\ r_{y}'(t) & =2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquare each derivative component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S_{x} & =16 \\cos^{2}{\\left(2 t \\right)} \\\\ S_{y} & =4 \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\| & =\\sqrt{S_x+S_y} \\\\  & =2 \\sqrt{\\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 4 \\cos^{2}{\\left(2 t \\right)}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRetain the parameter bounds and integrate the speed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}2 \\sqrt{\\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 4 \\cos^{2}{\\left(2 t \\right)}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712675 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ef03f71-66ed-5718-a233-9d27be50889c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{9 t^{2} + 18 t + 31} e^{t}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712651} {:answer/id #uuid "65414cf4-5a9e-5e92-bf84-752bdbdf76f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{9 t^{2} + 18 t + 22} e^{t}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712658} {:answer/id #uuid "94dc0ce5-f8cd-5cb1-be8f-a65ccfee64fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{9 t^{2} + 18 t + 13} e^{t}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712667} {:answer/id #uuid "95e8f283-c25d-5447-9e16-fd927c35b6d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{22} e^{t}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712668} {:answer/id #uuid "a6be7c3d-e448-51a4-bb22-438b8eafcffa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{9 t^{2} + 18 t + 9 \\left(t + 1\\right)^{2} + 22} e^{t}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712669}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65414cf4-5a9e-5e92-bf84-752bdbdf76f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{9 t^{2} + 18 t + 22} e^{t}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712658} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac389046-a6c7-519d-af8c-78302f041e86" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712671}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c5b7f27e-5e10-5894-ab3c-9dca13e15a30" :question/problem "Which integral expression gives the arc length of the curve\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=(- 2 e^{t})\\,i+(3 t e^{t})\\,j+(- 3 e^{t})\\,k\n$$\nfrom $t=-1$ to $t=1$? Do not evaluate the integral." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate each coordinate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r_{x}'(t) & =- 2 e^{t} \\\\ r_{y}'(t) & =3 \\left(t + 1\\right) e^{t} \\\\ r_{z}'(t) & =- 3 e^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquare each derivative component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S_{x} & =4 e^{2 t} \\\\ S_{y} & =9 t^{2} e^{2 t} + 18 t e^{2 t} + 9 e^{2 t} \\\\ S_{z} & =9 e^{2 t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\| & =\\sqrt{S_x+S_y+S_z} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9 t^{2} + 18 t + 22} e^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere $\\sqrt{e^{2t}}=e^t$ because $e^t>0$; the product square contributes $9 \\left(t + 1\\right)^{2}$ inside the remaining radical.\n\nRetain the parameter bounds and integrate the speed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =\\int_{-1}^{1}\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\  & =\\int_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{9 t^{2} + 18 t + 22} e^{t}\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712682 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35210161-a7b9-5806-a214-cea386c6055c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\pi}2\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712655} {:answer/id #uuid "900c63c1-6af4-550c-a953-27195015c9c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\pi}2 \\sqrt{6}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712666} {:answer/id #uuid "e6a04349-fa0c-5b2f-b3c2-669c8bbbb05c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\pi}2 \\sqrt{10}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712677} {:answer/id #uuid "f3ad6625-7bbc-5dc5-a599-ad600bd385ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\pi}2 \\sqrt{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712679} {:answer/id #uuid "fba9e043-e5ba-5f20-9091-5ac0e500d47c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\pi}\\sqrt{20}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712683}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fba9e043-e5ba-5f20-9091-5ac0e500d47c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\pi}\\sqrt{20}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712683} :answer-field/id #uuid "dae75a1b-d35a-5f1d-8fbb-ca9f5f67c952" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712676}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fb1544bc-3533-5bdd-9586-5646b5797802" :question/problem "Which integral expression gives the arc length of the curve\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=(2 t)\\,i+(- 2 \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)})\\,j+(- 2 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)})\\,k\n$$\nfrom $t=0$ to $t=\\pi$? Do not evaluate the integral.\n\n![The curve segment, parameter endpoints, and direction of travel.](images/24/24e8da3e728610a5ec6cdcbfe2c4b91aaba8ffe8b1cd218f7566a6cc238d2add.png)" :question/worked-solution "Differentiate each coordinate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r_{x}'(t) & =2 \\\\ r_{y}'(t) & =4 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)} \\\\ r_{z}'(t) & =- 4 \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquare each derivative component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S_{x} & =4 \\\\ S_{y} & =16 \\sin^{2}{\\left(2 t \\right)} \\\\ S_{z} & =16 \\cos^{2}{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombine paired squares using $\\sin^2(2 t)+\\cos^2(2 t)=1$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\| & =\\sqrt{S_x+S_y+S_z} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{20}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRetain the parameter bounds and integrate the speed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =\\int_{0}^{\\pi}\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{\\pi}\\sqrt{20}\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712709 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31aaef6b-d852-5f58-83f0-140a7a3c0f79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712715} {:answer/id #uuid "4c9bb9e2-0689-58c7-b3ae-c77d3f769832" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712722} {:answer/id #uuid "4e4f230a-4b61-5ff1-a208-e7fb5a0fe4df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712723} {:answer/id #uuid "a7d7cce3-7ed2-5576-8317-1fc7e2d2ee8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712733} {:answer/id #uuid "fab8afd8-4ac9-51cd-b6c9-14fcd19e100d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712741}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4c9bb9e2-0689-58c7-b3ae-c77d3f769832" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712722} :answer-field/id #uuid "b108234a-2613-5b3b-bb3b-548615871f7c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712734}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0f55ff81-8b03-569c-87d0-15b62bfa9f3f" :question/problem "Find the arc length of the curve with coordinate functions\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t)&=\\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\\\ y(t)&=\\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\\\ z(t)&=- t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfrom $t=-3$ to $t=0$." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate the coordinates and simplify the speed. Use $\\sin^2 t+\\cos^2 t=1$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x'(t)&=- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\\\ y'(t)&=\\cos{\\left(t \\right)} \\\\ z'(t)&=-1 \\\\ \\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|^2&=\\left(- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)^2 \\\\ &\\quad+\\left(\\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)^2+\\left(-1\\right)^2 \\\\ &=2 \\\\ \\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{2} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L&=\\int_{-3}^{0}\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ &=\\int_{-3}^{0}(\\sqrt{2})\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ &=\\left[\\sqrt{2} t\\right]_{-3}^{0} \\\\ &=\\left(0\\right)-\\left(- 3\\sqrt{2}\\right) \\\\ &=3\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712716 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f0dd84d-5151-5682-99e8-4c2da7d4f572" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712708} {:answer/id #uuid "8817ede7-76c7-5822-9021-a4568276c28d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{488}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712725} {:answer/id #uuid "93dbe923-add9-5454-8ddb-899d041b5897" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712728} {:answer/id #uuid "a3abfc7b-18b5-5b2c-8952-68afebda3c7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712731} {:answer/id #uuid "c18017b3-ed3c-5d57-8ca8-a13404e675f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 16\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712737}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3abfc7b-18b5-5b2c-8952-68afebda3c7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712731} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2057e79-b4ae-5857-9f06-bb6eb6b88b22" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712729}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "32b1249f-c11f-5956-97cc-7bdafc6c1610" :question/problem "Find the arc length of the curve with coordinate functions\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t)&=2 \\\\ y(t)&=- t^{2} \\\\ z(t)&=t^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfrom $t=4$ to $t=5$." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate the coordinates and simplify the speed. Since $t\\ge 0$ on this interval, $|t|=t$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x'(t)&=0 \\\\ y'(t)&=- 2 t \\\\ z'(t)&=2 t \\\\ \\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|^2&=\\left(0\\right)^2 \\\\ &\\quad+\\left(- 2 t\\right)^2+\\left(2 t\\right)^2 \\\\ &=8 t^{2} \\\\ \\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{8 t^{2}} \\\\ &=2\\sqrt{2}|t| \\\\ &=2\\sqrt{2} t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L&=\\int_{4}^{5}\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ &=\\int_{4}^{5}(2\\sqrt{2} t)\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ &=\\left[\\sqrt{2} t^{2}\\right]_{4}^{5} \\\\ &=\\left(25\\sqrt{2}\\right)-\\left(16\\sqrt{2}\\right) \\\\ &=9\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712730 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "226aa542-b31e-5d75-aec5-05f25414e3fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712710} {:answer/id #uuid "2774acc8-3210-5e03-8722-42128c7970c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712711} {:answer/id #uuid "30d3100f-658d-5b49-8469-59ebfb2ae6b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{39}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712714} {:answer/id #uuid "355f8415-b6fd-51f2-acb3-077005a2a882" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712718} {:answer/id #uuid "4c6987d6-ff42-5586-b89b-46a3d16b3e62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712721}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4c6987d6-ff42-5586-b89b-46a3d16b3e62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712721} :answer-field/id #uuid "03be8a1e-5a4b-517d-a714-5653e8ed607c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712707}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a28e9361-0bfe-5283-921f-b3bc8b4db3e4" :question/problem "Find the arc length of the curve with coordinate functions\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t)&=t^{2} - 4 \\\\ y(t)&=\\frac{t^{2}}{2} - 2 \\\\ z(t)&=- t^{2} - 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfrom $t=-3$ to $t=-2$." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate the coordinates and simplify the speed. Since $t\\le 0$ on this interval, $|t|=-t$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x'(t)&=2 t \\\\ y'(t)&=t \\\\ z'(t)&=- 2 t \\\\ \\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|^2&=\\left(2 t\\right)^2 \\\\ &\\quad+\\left(t\\right)^2+\\left(- 2 t\\right)^2 \\\\ &=9 t^{2} \\\\ \\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{9 t^{2}} \\\\ &=3|t| \\\\ &=- 3 t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L&=\\int_{-3}^{-2}\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ &=\\int_{-3}^{-2}(- 3 t)\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ &=\\left[- \\frac{3 t^{2}}{2}\\right]_{-3}^{-2} \\\\ &=\\left(-6\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{27}{2}\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{15}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712738 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28ead7fe-3aa4-5364-8a40-7123bd2adb21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{68}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712713} {:answer/id #uuid "4361d31f-97e8-58fd-8a0b-9a849a8255de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712720} {:answer/id #uuid "b4a1966c-83e8-5a68-939c-89431f94e677" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712735} {:answer/id #uuid "c0bca2f2-cf79-577d-bf21-b7b71e8f506f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{20}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712736} {:answer/id #uuid "ca27b478-2270-5531-8a63-50eac50ef56d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712739}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "28ead7fe-3aa4-5364-8a40-7123bd2adb21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{68}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712713} :answer-field/id #uuid "27eb5d50-064c-5877-9129-d882f86a270b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712712}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c907927b-d046-56a9-a4d3-28ad63843ee0" :question/problem "Find the arc length of the curve with coordinate functions\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t)&=- 2 t \\\\ y(t)&=t^{2} \\\\ z(t)&=2 - \\frac{t^{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfrom $t=2$ to $t=4$." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate the coordinates and simplify the speed. The quadratic inside the square is positive for every real $t$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x'(t)&=-2 \\\\ y'(t)&=2 t \\\\ z'(t)&=- t^{2} \\\\ \\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|^2&=\\left(-2\\right)^2 \\\\ &\\quad+\\left(2 t\\right)^2+\\left(- t^{2}\\right)^2 \\\\ &=t^{4} + 4 t^{2} + 4 \\\\ \\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{t^{4} + 4 t^{2} + 4} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{\\left(t^{2} + 2\\right)^2} \\\\ &=t^{2} + 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L&=\\int_{2}^{4}\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ &=\\int_{2}^{4}(t^{2} + 2)\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ &=\\left[\\frac{t \\left(t^{2} + 6\\right)}{3}\\right]_{2}^{4} \\\\ &=\\left(\\frac{88}{3}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{20}{3}\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{68}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712740 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34a80d96-717c-5211-9749-fce6fd92a099" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712717} {:answer/id #uuid "7a093a9e-be34-5efc-b5c4-dba81fca3eb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8376}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712724} {:answer/id #uuid "8950632b-701e-543b-ac19-befa8a66dd37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{10470}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712726} {:answer/id #uuid "920067b2-cde6-57ac-92df-da6ffde37032" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712727} {:answer/id #uuid "a5b882cb-7145-5c84-81c0-f5af0ae1642e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712732}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a5b882cb-7145-5c84-81c0-f5af0ae1642e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712732} :answer-field/id #uuid "400520fa-a8b9-5366-bd25-97a4275d4f67" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712719}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e53d755e-be18-536b-a74b-89e4ba254c23" :question/problem "Find the arc length of the curve with coordinate functions\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t)&=\\sqrt{6} t^{2} - 4\\sqrt{2} + 2 \\\\ y(t)&=- 2 t - 8 \\\\ z(t)&=2 - 2 t^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfrom $t=2$ to $t=3$." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate the coordinates and simplify the speed. The quadratic inside the square is positive for every real $t$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x'(t)&=2\\sqrt{6} t \\\\ y'(t)&=-2 \\\\ z'(t)&=- 6 t^{2} \\\\ \\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|^2&=\\left(2\\sqrt{6} t\\right)^2 \\\\ &\\quad+\\left(-2\\right)^2+\\left(- 6 t^{2}\\right)^2 \\\\ &=36 t^{4} + 24 t^{2} + 4 \\\\ \\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{36 t^{4} + 24 t^{2} + 4} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{\\left(6 t^{2} + 2\\right)^2} \\\\ &=6 t^{2} + 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L&=\\int_{2}^{3}\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ &=\\int_{2}^{3}(6 t^{2} + 2)\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ &=\\left[2 t \\left(t^{2} + 1\\right)\\right]_{2}^{3} \\\\ &=\\left(60\\right)-\\left(20\\right) \\\\ &=40\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712747 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b1f7512-614d-5707-aa55-fca67e170580" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712744} {:answer/id #uuid "44916d95-df77-53c7-843c-efa29755be73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712750} {:answer/id #uuid "4aa4b43f-d78d-5da2-b1e8-942ee5461aef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712752} {:answer/id #uuid "8a7b5f1c-f019-5e1e-ac7d-8bfd7abca5b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712756} {:answer/id #uuid "8ff128ff-5593-5a84-a022-72ebd7e3a57d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "170" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712759}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b1f7512-614d-5707-aa55-fca67e170580" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712744} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a3c46f6-a99e-5b46-9f80-8870c3e34645" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712755}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "28746818-9927-55b6-bab6-fa7bff59ea12" :question/problem "Find the arc length of the curve with coordinate functions\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t)&=4 t \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)} + 2 \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)} \\\\ y(t)&=3 t^{2} + 2 \\\\ z(t)&=4 t \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)} - 2 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfrom $t=3$ to $t=5$." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate the coordinates and simplify the speed. Since $t\\ge 0$ on this interval, $|t|=t$. Use $\\sin^2(\\theta)+\\cos^2(\\theta)=1$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x'(t)&=2\\left(2\\sin(2t)+4t\\cos(2t)-2\\sin(2t)\\right) \\\\ &=8 t \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)} \\\\ y'(t)&=6 t \\\\ z'(t)&=2\\left(2\\cos(2t)-4t\\sin(2t)-2\\cos(2t)\\right) \\\\ &=- 8 t \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)} \\\\ \\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|^2&=\\left(8 t \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right)^2 \\\\ &\\quad+\\left(6 t\\right)^2+\\left(- 8 t \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right)^2 \\\\ &=100 t^{2} \\\\ \\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{100 t^{2}} \\\\ &=10|t| \\\\ &=10 t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L&=\\int_{3}^{5}\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ &=\\int_{3}^{5}(10 t)\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ &=\\left[5 t^{2}\\right]_{3}^{5} \\\\ &=\\left(125\\right)-\\left(45\\right) \\\\ &=80\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712757 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1dbf99c5-89fa-5c97-b7f0-b23e0a29d363" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712745} {:answer/id #uuid "22492c65-fba0-5ad4-8212-67f73f85440a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712746} {:answer/id #uuid "3f35bde6-05bc-5b22-9ce8-e0847994686a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{45}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712749} {:answer/id #uuid "92dccf95-1543-594e-b3fd-1695bc3ea559" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "90" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712760} {:answer/id #uuid "da0fc24f-60f2-512d-8723-2f4e358c75f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712766}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "22492c65-fba0-5ad4-8212-67f73f85440a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712746} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b9ba254-5025-5c79-a902-823930ca334b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712743}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8e96c242-2624-5661-b28b-c6a6e4add163" :question/problem "Find the arc length of the curve with coordinate functions\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t)&=- 4 t \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)} + 2 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)} - 2 \\\\ y(t)&=- 4 t \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)} - 2 \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)} - 2 \\\\ z(t)&=3 t^{2} + 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfrom $t=0$ to $t=3$." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate the coordinates and simplify the speed. Since $t\\ge 0$ on this interval, $|t|=t$. Use $\\sin^2(\\theta)+\\cos^2(\\theta)=1$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x'(t)&=-2\\left(2\\cos(2t)-4t\\sin(2t)-2\\cos(2t)\\right) \\\\ &=8 t \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)} \\\\ y'(t)&=-2\\left(2\\sin(2t)+4t\\cos(2t)-2\\sin(2t)\\right) \\\\ &=- 8 t \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)} \\\\ z'(t)&=6 t \\\\ \\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|^2&=\\left(8 t \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right)^2 \\\\ &\\quad+\\left(- 8 t \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right)^2+\\left(6 t\\right)^2 \\\\ &=100 t^{2} \\\\ \\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{100 t^{2}} \\\\ &=10|t| \\\\ &=10 t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L&=\\int_{0}^{3}\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{3}(10 t)\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ &=\\left[5 t^{2}\\right]_{0}^{3} \\\\ &=\\left(45\\right)-\\left(0\\right) \\\\ &=45\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
